Date: Mon,  7 Nov 1994 18:38:07 -0500
Message-ID: <cijfdT_00iVDM_SnVD@andrew.cmu.edu>

This is the message I just posted to some internal CMU newsgroups.

-Declan

---

I just came from a meeting with Robert Mehrabian, and this is what he's
decided, based on the letter I sent him and input from a group of
students, faculty, and staff at the meeting:

* Create a standing committee to decide what newsgroups to remove or reinstate
* Remove the binaries newsgroups tomorrow as planned then review their removal
* NOT remove the text newsgroups tomorrow (alt.sex, rec.arts.erotica)

The standing committee will have about eight people on it, and will do
two things:

* Investigate which of the removed binaries newsgroups we can legally carry
* Respond to complaints about individual text bboards by considering if
we can legally carry them

Members of the committee will be appointed by Student Government,
Faculty Senate, and Staff Council in order to represent the entire
University community. Ex-Officio members will probably include the Dean
of Student Affairs, the VP of Computing Services, the University
Librarian, and lawyers chosen by the University and the members of the
committee.

In my opinion, this is a good start. While I support carrying all
newgroups in general, the University wants to remove the binaries
newsgroups, and they have some pretty good reasons -- Universities have
been in legal trouble in the past for carrying them. Even the EFF agrees
that the binaries newsgroups are probably illegal.

Also, we're having a Freedom in Cyberspace rally on Wednesday at noon on
the steps of Warner Hall, and Mike Godwin is planned as the keynote
speaker. Godwin is a columnist for Wired and Internet World, and
staff counsel for EFF. PSFB will be sponsoring his visit.

A reminder: There will be a Student Senate meeting tonight at 7 pm in
Wean Hall 7500. We're also going to get together at 10 pm tonight in the
same room to discuss planning for the rally; everyone is invited to
attend and help out.

Sincerely,

Declan McCullagh
President of the Student Body

