    So what's your point ? That because YOU grew up watching violent shows,
    and did not turn out too bad, that any kid who DOES turn out badly, is
    that way because of bad parenting ? That is a very simplistic and wrong
    conclusion to draw. The reasons why any particular child grows up with
    anti-social tendancies are varied and complex. But the effects of T.V.
    on children have been much studied, and I don't think that there
    is much doubt that there are definite observable effects on the aggressiveness
    of children: studies repeatedly show that children's play tends to be
    much more violent after watching violent T.V. shows, than after watching
    non-violent T.V. shows. Now, one may not be able to predict exactly which
    children will become seriously anti-social as a result, but it is surely not
    unreasonable to draw the conclusion that, STATISTICALLY, there is a strong
    argument that T.V. violence is at least a contributing factor to the anti-social
    behaviour of some people. 

