the street when we tell them not to, play games we forbid and say words 
we deem unacceptable for little gentlemen and ladies. But you'll find 
that if you expect a standard of behavior, reinforce it, mete out 
punishment when appropreate and (this is sneaky, but works wonderfully) 
commend them on their behavior when you see the guilty look in their 
eyes. You've got to have set them up with some sense of responsibility 
beforehand for this to work, but it reinforces the concept of behavior 
for behavior's sake, rather than to not get caught.
