abstain. If they'd do it just because you're not there to catch them, I'd 
ask myself how you expect these kids to handle more serious moral 
dilemmas when they get older.
  It's not a matter of dictating to them every choice in their lives, but 
rather setting them up with a moral guideline for their lives. Are you 
dictating when you tell them to never steal? Never kill? Why is never 
watch tv more offensive? "Are you able to not watch tv? I'd wager you 
your not being able to do without tv at all."
  And if you set up this kind of supportive environment, you'll easily be 
able to educate them on the right and wrong of the tv they do see.

