  You're unfortunately right, too many places that SHOULDN'T be tv rooms 
have become so. But I will assure you it can be dealt with. Here's how:
 1) Make it clear to the places where your kids are watched outside of 
school, be it after-school programs, activity groups and so on, that your 
kids aren't allowed to watch television without you. They'll look at you 
funny to be sure, but if they refuse to accomidate your wishes on those 
rare occasionals where they show tv (and if it's not rare, find a new 
place for your kids or just give up and leave 'em home - at least they 
